WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.580
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский, эпизод 40, 415 июня 2026 года.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.400
I'm allia, and we've got some great Russian words to learn today.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.880
Поехали, let's go.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.280
Our word of the day is poest.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.660
Oh yes, say it slowly with me.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.940
Oh yes, it means frame.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.060
Imagine a long vehicle on tracks that carries you across the country.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.500
The memory hook is that it sounds a bit like poest,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.080
but it takes you far away on an adventure.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.920
Repeat after me, poest.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.620
Now use it in a sentence.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:37.520
Я you do na poезде, that means I am going by train.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.020
Let's build more words for our journey.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.740
Our first new word is samolot.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.780
Samolot, it means airplane.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.220
Repeat after me.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.820
Samolot, samolot starts with Samo like same,

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.320
because the same sky belongs to everyone.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:56.320
The airplane flies high, or samolot летит гусако.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.080
Next comes bilet.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:58.760
Билет.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:00:59.760
It means ticket.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:00.920
Repeat after me.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:01.660
Билет.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.440
Picture a little B that lets you on to the plane.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:05.760
Where is my ticket?

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.100
Or where is my bilet?

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.820
Now we need something to pack.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:09.460
Чемодан.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:10.260
Чемодан.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:11.080
It means suitcase.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:12.480
Repeat after me.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:13.140
Чемодан.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.220
Imagine a chemical dance stuffing his back full of clothes.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.800
My suitcase is heavy.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:18.800
Or more.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:19.920
Чемодан тяжелый.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.320
Where do we catch the train?

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.260
От вокзал.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:22.940
вокзал.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.160
It means train station.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.420
Repeat after me.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:26.180
вокзал.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.160
Think of вокзал.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.420
The place you walk to before boarding.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.180
We are at train station.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.820
Or мы на вокзале.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.440
Do not forget your passport.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:35.360
Passport.

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:36.340
It means passport.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.800
Repeat after me.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:38.520
Passport.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.560
This one is almost the same as the English word.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:42.980
So it isn't easy win.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.220
Show your passport.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:45.520
Or покажи passport.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.780
Our big word for today is путешествие.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:49.700
путешествие.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.520
It means journey or trip.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:52.700
Repeat after me.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:16.940
путешествие.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.320
пут your share on aствие at venture.

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:21.040
And you

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.500
Remember it.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:28.460
На самолете, means by airplane, the ending of the word changes after now, but the idea

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.280
stay simple.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:35.620
Now, you can say, я еду на поисде, and we fly by airplane, or mildly team на самолете.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.640
Long train rides are a favorite Russian tradition.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.100
Families bring tea in special glasses with metal holders.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.640
Passengers often chat with strangers in the same compartment.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.020
The hours on the train turn into friendly conversations and shared stories.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.880
Remember Koshka from a few lessons ago?

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:53.980
And Sabaka?

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.440
Great job connecting old words to new travel adventures.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.720
For kids, draw a train, plane and suitcase.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.240
Then label each one while saying the Russian word out loud.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.920
For adults, stand at an imaginary airport, and practice with themoy billet three times.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.180
Then say, мой чима дан тяжери три more times.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.720
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.020
Want to know a secret about billet?

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:24.480
Did you know that the Russian word billet and the English word ticket are actually cousins?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:29.420
They both come from the same old French route that started as a little Latin label.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:34.500
The word traveled through French as billet and reached Russia in the 1700s.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.700
When Peter the Great was improving travel.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:41.180
Watch out though, because billet can also mean an exam paper in school.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.380
So the sentence around it tells you if it is for a train or a test.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.740
Next time you hold a ticket, remember it shares a story with billet.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.640
And that little Latin label is your secret shortcut to remembering the word forever.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.200
You did great today.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.680
Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.960
Share the show with a friend who wants to learn Russian and I'll see you next time.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:04.520
Пока!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:09.600
And if you'd rather watch than listen, find us on YouTube at etenera.ru.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.080
Links in the show notes.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.640
This release sounds with the help of Yisint Zagolosa.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.520
I'll see you next time with a friend.
